    <div id="MainContentPlaceholder_T80CFEFCC002_Col01" class="sf_colsIn col-sm-8 main-content" data-sf-element="Column 2" data-placeholder-label="Area: Content Area"><article id="MainContentPlaceholder_T80CFEFCC003_Col00" class="sf_colsIn dynamic-nav-content" data-sf-element="Article" data-placeholder-label="Area: Article Area">
    
    <h2>Educational resources for financial professionals</h2><p>In support of the work of the Central Bank Climate Risk and Sustainable Finance Forum, the Capacity Building Working Group has compiled a comprehensive list of courses to aid financial sector professionals in understanding climate-related financial risks and sustainable finance practices.<br /></p>
    
   



<div class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9">
    <iframe src="/placeholder.html" data-src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/iUbhKQcgk-U?si=g-P2g6JlB5O51DY8rel=0" aria-label="Video within iFrame" title="Video iFrame" class="optanon-category-C0004 embed-responsive-item" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div>




<div class="panel panel-default standard-accordion">
    <div class="panel-heading" id="heading-Climate-Change-Training-Directory-f74f3b1f-9d27-44a9-b733-449bfd860068">
        <div class="panel-title">
            <a class="collapsed gtm-expanding" role="button" data-toggle="collapse" href="#Climate-Change-Training-Directory-f74f3b1f-9d27-44a9-b733-449bfd860068" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="Climate-Change-Training-Directory-f74f3b1f-9d27-44a9-b733-449bfd860068">
                <strong class="gtm-expanding">Climate Change Training Directory</strong>
                    <small>
                        Video Transcript
                    </small>

            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div id="Climate-Change-Training-Directory-f74f3b1f-9d27-44a9-b733-449bfd860068" class="panel-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-Climate-Change-Training-Directory-f74f3b1f-9d27-44a9-b733-449bfd860068">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <p><strong>Kevin Thompson, CEO Intact Ireland, Former Co-Chair:</strong> The Sustainability Working Group was established to build awareness within the financial service sector regarding climate change and to help build capacity to meet the challenges presented
    by climate change.</p>
<p><strong>Aedin O'Leary, Boards, Asset Management &amp; Funds:</strong> Well, I think sustainable finance is fundamentally changing the way investment decisions are made today. And in today's world, investment teams, advisors, and boards need to know more
    about the landscape in which they're operating around sustainable investment and understanding ESG risks and opportunities.</p>
<p><strong>Diarmuid Murphy, Institute of Bankers</strong>:Capital is definitely needed in terms of financing the transition, but it's also the skills, competencies, and the judgment to apply that capital to financing the transition.</p>
<p><strong>Anne McGlynn, Insurance Institute:</strong> ESG literacy is so important. Just recently, the ECB published a report that shows that climate change has already impacted on global GDP by 20%. So it's imperative for us that are working in financial
    services that we understand that impact.
</p>
<p><strong>Diarmuid Murphy, Institute of Bankers:</strong>IOB supports professionals and boards in terms of their lifelong learning, and this is something that's facilitated by IOB-supported skills framework.</p>

<p><strong>Aidan Flynn, Insurance Ireland:</strong> We really want to encourage all within the financial sector to get involved, build capacity, build more sustainability and climate risk training, because we all must play our part.</p>
<p><strong>Anne McGlynn, Insurance Institute:</strong> So it's perfect timing that we have this new resource, this inventory of programs and qualifications, which is hosted on the Central Bank website, so that we can upskill our members in this really critical
    area of climate change.</p>
<p><strong>Elizabeth SmithWright, Brokers Ireland:</strong>We believe continued investment in education is crucial for our brokers and their employees. It ensures that they remain competent and confident in advising their customers in relation to sustainability.</p>
<p><strong>David Delaney Sustainability Professiona</strong><strong>l:</strong>ESG studies have been very beneficial to me in my career in asset management in terms of setting up our risk frameworks to ensure proper implementation of regulatory requirements,
    meeting ESG requirements on a day-to-day basis, communicating expectations across the business and to our investors in an informed way.</p>
<p><strong>Tracey Mullin Ryan, Sustainability Professional:</strong> It can be challenging to find courses within the ESG space, and it would've been very helpful to have an inventory of ESG courses available to me.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

    
    <p>Whether you are building foundational knowledge or advancing your expertise, these resources offer a range of flexible learning options to suit financial professionals who would like to build their skills in this critical area of our financial system.</p>
    
   

    
    <h2>In Person</h2>
<div class="table-wrapper">
    <table class="table-dark k-table" summary="Table 1: QB4 December 2025 Forecast Summary and Revisions from September 2025 Baseline Projections" tabindex="0" style="width:820px;">
